  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only existing color-level claim, object search and approach, pickup, matching-zone search and approach, drop, publication, and team reception events. Red is represented as three one-box batches, green as a two-box batch followed by one box, and blue as one three-box batch. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because search_object, approach_object, search_zone, and approach_zone are the required task-level movement requests, while the fixed collision_avoidance specification remains responsible for safe motion. Release events are omitted because abandoning a claim attempt occurs before ownership is acquired, and releasing a successfully claimed color would permit another robot to take the same assignment.",
    "transition_design": "select_color repeatedly enables search_object and enters r_claim, g_claim, or b_claim only after the matching object-visible observation. Each claim-attempt state handles the corresponding received_claim event by abandoning that branch. Search and approach actions are repeatable self-loops, visibility loss returns to the relevant search state, and reached observations advance from both search and approach states. Pickup and drop requests are enabled only after matching reached observations, with failed confirmations returning to recovery search states. The counter-state sequences enforce red batches of one, a green batch of two followed by one, and a blue batch of three; one drop unloads each represented batch. Publication occurs only after all three boxes assigned to that color have confirmed delivery, since the fixed availability automata make a published color permanently delivered. The wait states collect the other two delivered-color observations, and only all_done is marked. No low-level motion or collision behavior is added or overridden.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
  }
